                                "sense_id": "db3f1c7a-be27-3ce0-ab34-af02dcef5c53",
                                "text": "Ignorance implies real indifference, however copious the wordmongering."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b790bc4-61c3-43d4-9ead-726eb32a5385",
                                "sense_id": "db3f1c7a-be27-3ce0-ab34-af02dcef5c53",
                                "text": "Powers are seeking as before to drown the problem of disarmament in endless and futile wordmongering."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d594e1b9-de0d-46dc-a014-168197fc1fc5",
                                "sense_id": "db3f1c7a-be27-3ce0-ab34-af02dcef5c53",
                                "text": "Melville \"repels\" here; he is guilty of \"wordmongering,\" prolixity, and recourse to \"marvellous\" yarns that erode what is usefully \"probable\" in the narrative."
                            }
                        ]
